# Byte-exact evidence files.
#
# evidence/preregistration.json and evidence/meta.json are evidence artifacts, not source. Their
# SHA-256 values are recorded in evidence/EVIDENCE-MANIFEST.md and published as release assets, so a
# checkout that rewrites their line endings hashes differently from the published value and the
# verification fails on that platform.
#
# The two were frozen with different endings, so `-text` (no end-of-line conversion on commit or
# checkout) keeps each exactly as published:
#
#   evidence/preregistration.json   CRLF   sha256 50e4adde...
#   evidence/meta.json              LF     sha256 5a0ea059...
#
# Both directions of the problem are real here. With core.autocrlf=true, preregistration.json is
# rewritten to LF when committed, and meta.json is rewritten to CRLF when checked out. Both files are
# attested by hash, so both must be stored and checked out exactly as they are, on every platform.
evidence/preregistration.json -text
evidence/meta.json -text
